= Feedback loop =
A feedback loop is a circular causal process in which the output or state of a system influences subsequent inputs or behavior of that same system.

== Negative feedback ==
Negative feedback counteracts deviation and can stabilize a system around a range or target. Many homeostatic mechanisms use negative feedback.

== Positive feedback ==
Positive feedback reinforces change and can amplify a process until another constraint, resource limit, or control mechanism intervenes.

== Importance ==
Feedback is central to cybernetics, physiology, ecology, engineering, economics, computation, and organizational behavior because it connects system state to future system behavior.

